2)a. Write a HTML program, to explain the working of tables.
 (use tags: <table><><><> and attributes: border, rowspan, colspan) .
<!DOCTYPE html>
<head>
<title>Table Example</title>
<style>
table {
border-collapse: collapse;
width: 70%;
margin: 20px auto;
font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
}
th,
td {
border: 1px solid #333;
padding: 10px;
text-align: center;
}
th {
background-color: #f4f4f4;
}
</style>
</head>
<body>
<h1 style="text-align: center;">HTML Table Example</h1>
<table border="1">
<!-- Table Header -->
<tr>
<th>Item</th>
<th>Category</th>
<th colspan="2">Details</th>
</tr>

<!-- Table Body -->
<tr>
<td rowspan="2">Laptop</td>
<td>Electronics</td>
<td>Brand</td>
<td>Apple</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Price</td>
<td>$1200</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td rowspan="2">Chair</td>
<td>Furniture</td>
<td>Material</td>
<td>Wood</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Price</td>
<td>$150</td>
</tr>
</table>
</body>
</html>
